[h3]Raiding Focus[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Token Abduction[/b] (new focus): capped at 5% of a target's population. Completing a raid grants 12 months of your unity income. There is no escalation ladder. Once the cap is reached, your only option is to switch to plundering their worlds instead.
[*][b]Reaping[/b] is now the default only for the civics built around it: Harvesting Protocol, Harvest Incorporated and Ravager Swarm. Other empires that qualify still get it as a choice.
[*]Pop raiding is now called [b]Abduction[/b], keeping it distinct from [b]Plunder[/b] on the resource side. Robot Raiding's first option now reads [b]Organics and Robots[/b].
[/list]

[h3]Despoliation Traditions[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Forward Raiding Base[/b] reworked. It no longer skims 3% from every nearby colony each cycle. Instead, each non-ally colony within 3 systems has a 1 in 12 chance per cycle of being raided for 60% of a month's output.
[/list]

[h3]Privateer Enclave[/h3]
[list]
[*]Nomads can now be privateer patrons. Patronage is positional: the system's owner and any nomad holding a waystation in that system both count, and an enclave can have one of each. Both are paid dividends independently.
[*]An enclave left with no patron at all now stops cycling instead of running dividends with nobody to pay.
[/list]

[h3]Fixes[/h3]
[list]
[*]The raiding report no longer appears when a war ends.
[*]The opportunistic raiding prompt no longer appears twice for the same target.
[*]Raiding is no longer blocked when you declare a new war on an empire you recently fought.
[/list]
